WEBVTT

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:17.410
Damn... I thought they'd fly us straight to Babylon.

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:21.680
It's a shame, but the dragons can't stray too far from their home.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.450
Hopefully, any hunters can't find them.

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.690
I'd like to get back to my own home, too...

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:31.760
You're always so homesick, aren't you?

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.960
N-No I'm not!

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:34.730
Really?

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:36.890
You don't know what you're talking about.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:44.570
Trapped by a Warp Relic...

00:00:52.980 --> 00:01:02.960
<i>In the city without love</i> <i>only your smile remains.</i>

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:12.960
<i>Hold me tight to crush the loneliness,</i> <i>it's all that stops these pains.</i>

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:23.350
<i>You're constrained by that limit.</i>
<i>Free yourself and break apart the chains.</i>

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:33.340
<i>It's all gonna burn on down.</i>
<i>Dance to the flames that consume the night.</i>

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:43.520
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright.</i>

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:54.040
<i>Dance to the end of the night.</i>

00:01:54.040 --> 00:02:04.040
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright. Dance!</i>

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:14.730
<i>In the city without love</i>

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:31.050
We're not far now from Babylon.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.650
We're getting down to the home stretch.

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:37.890
Hey... We haven't run into
Delzaine this whole time.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:41.060
Do you think he might have beat us there?

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:45.730
It's hard to say. He took a different route than we did.

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:49.730
What if he gets there first and does something to Babel?

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:54.040
Will that mean my ride back home is gone?

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.710
Either way, we need to stop him from using Babel.

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:02.870
If he's so obsessed with the surface, it's probably not for a good reason.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:12.760
What's wrong, Eljuia?

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:14.190
Eljuia!

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:23.060
"10: Feelings"

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:29.070
He woke up!

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:33.980
Phew! You had us all scared when you fell over like that.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.950
What happened, Eljuia?

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:40.820
I sense that the upcoming events are very...

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.440
...very ominous.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:44.790
Another omen?

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:49.790
Yes. The powers preserving
Endora are being lost...

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:52.730
The world is verging on destruction.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:54.460
What do you mean?

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:56.830
I do not know, however...

00:03:56.830 --> 00:04:01.840
Whatever happens may be terrible beyond belief.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:04.940
Terrible beyond belief?
What's that supposed to mean?

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:08.840
The whole of Endora must be in danger in the future.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:10.750
Endora...

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:15.020
If only I knew the meaning of what I saw...

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:20.650
World destruction, huh? I can't even imagine something of that scale.

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:41.480
I've personally developed a method to restore Babel

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:44.650
through days of my own painstaking labor and research.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:47.720
It is only because of my superior intellect and talent that--

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.950
Just get to the point.

00:04:54.220 --> 00:05:01.700
We know how to restore Babel, but some time is needed to make last-minute adjustments.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:06.900
Very well. Compared to how long
I've waited thus far, a little longer matters not.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:12.680
But, my Lord, why is it that you're so engrossed with Babel?

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:18.010
I've worked on it so long, could you not tell me your objective?

00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:20.720
There is no need for you to know.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.480
But my Lord, I--

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:28.390
Do you want that badly to be relieved of your head?

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:35.730
How about cutting your subordinates some slack, my Lord?

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:37.530
It's those vile Zoozians!

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:40.240
You're in the King's presence!
Watch your mouth!

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:41.670
Eh?!

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:44.570
Quit it, Ibelda.

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:52.240
We've come to report in.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:59.960
So the Ignauts have allied with the island Zoozians...

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:04.930
Ibelda. It seems you haven't been following my orders.

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:06.900
What do you mean?

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:09.590
Who was it that gave you that scar?

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:14.700
If I recall, I ordered you to observe Emilio and the others.

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:17.640
Had I ever given you permission to engage?

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:24.810
I knew it. I can guess exactly what happened.

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:27.120
Damn. Can't fool 'em.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:31.450
Only do what I order you.
Refrain from anything else.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:41.430
Damn that Delzaine!

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:43.770
Agreed.

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:46.800
Relax. We all had that coming.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.970
You went too far, Ibelda.

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:51.440
Huh?! It's my fault now?!

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:56.650
Look at those savages...

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:58.250
Typical Zoozians...

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:01.410
Why would the King keep animals like them?

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:07.920
Which one of you wants to die first?

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:14.600
Don't. If you kill anyone, our position will be at risk.

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:18.870
It pisses me off...

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:22.970
Why do we have to put up with everyone's shit?!

00:07:22.970 --> 00:07:24.370
Agreed.

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:32.950
Now I'm curious why Delzaine is so obsessed with Babel and the surface.

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:35.540
I kinda want to know for myself...

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:49.800
From them again?

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:51.030
Yeah.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:55.300
The Ignauts are closing in on Babylon as well.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:07.220
Nearly all the materials regarding
Babel have been lost or destroyed...

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:12.480
The scant remains that are left are so obscured they're all but useless.

00:08:14.020 --> 00:08:16.760
What is the King trying to hide?

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:20.060
Why is he so fixated with Babel?

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:22.760
Too much remains a mystery...

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:28.670
It will be difficult to return Shun to the surface without knowing more about Babel...

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:30.500
There you are!

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:38.580
Sheesh! Running around the laboratory is such a waste of energy and time.

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:43.350
If only there was a way to get around more efficiently...

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:46.860
How about making the entire floor mobile?

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:49.760
Or perhaps making a self-propelled vehicle that--

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:52.790
I see! I'll work on the plans at once!

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:55.100
I'll start thinking about the parts and the energy!

00:08:55.100 --> 00:09:00.100
Oh, I know! If I can just rework the circuit
I recently made and increase the output--

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:02.800
Did you actually come for something?

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:06.610
Ah, yes. The regional Warp Particle measurements are complete.

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:08.610
The results arrive tomorrow.

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:14.750
The chief was against it, but I'm glad we sent people out to investigate again.

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:19.720
Yeah. It's great that you noticed an anomaly with the Warp Particles.

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:23.630
Your powers of observation and attention are well honed.

00:09:23.630 --> 00:09:26.830
It means so much to be praised by you!

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:32.170
I only noticed Warp Particles decreasing because of the new measuring device you invented.

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:34.170
When I saw the data, I had a flash of insight...

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:37.140
Warp Particles are a vital part of Endora.

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:41.840
If they suddenly deplete, the entirety of Endora will most certainly suffer...

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:52.250
This is getting out of hand...

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:55.490
All this stuff about Babel and what's happening to Endora...

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:59.030
Will I really be able to get back home?

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:01.690
I'll make sure you get to the surface.

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:06.440
These problems are Endora's, not yours.

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:09.710
So, you don't have to concern yourself.

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:12.270
Emilio, you...

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:13.280
Go to sleep.

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:15.270
Huh? Okay...

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:24.120
I guess he's got his own problems to worry about.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:28.460
His own father was killed and now he's obsessed with revenge.

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:32.230
And now the future of his world is uncertain...

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:33.660
Emilio.

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:38.300
Somehow or another, we've always stuck together.

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:42.170
I plan to help you all the way to the end.

00:10:42.170 --> 00:10:47.210
But... I still don't think it's right to kill for revenge.

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:49.340
Isn't there some other way?

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:54.140
Did he fall asleep?

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:03.820
You can't possibly understand...

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:10.190
You'll never... get past me...

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:17.410
Father... How can I stop Emilio from going through with it?

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:19.910
All right. The rest of the watch is yours.

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:20.410
Okay.

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:22.410
Oh? You're still awake?

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:23.950
Louise...

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:28.920
We're getting an early start tomorrow, so it'll be rough if you don't get sleep.

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:30.610
Yeah. You're right.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:35.860
Worried about something?

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:38.620
No... Good night.

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:11.330
Emilio...

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:12.130
Seriously?

00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:13.960
You couldn't have done better, Ralph.

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:18.130
This brings the Ignauts one step closer to victory.

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:20.470
Now it's only a matter of time.

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:23.440
We might not be able to face Delzaine head on, but--

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:25.140
You finally woke up?

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:27.340
Yeah... Who's this?

00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:29.510
You don't remember me?

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:36.520
He's one of the guys that went their own way after our base was attacked by the Truculent.

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:40.160
Oh yeah! I thought you looked familiar!

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:42.920
I was just one among the crowd.

00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:47.330
They ventured to lands far away from the capital.

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:50.530
That is, to gain the support of as many lords as they could.

00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:52.000
Indeed.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:56.610
There are many areas simply out of Delzaine's reach.

00:12:56.610 --> 00:13:01.180
Most of the lords we spoke with offered to lend us their support.

00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:03.850
Really? So you mean...

00:13:03.850 --> 00:13:08.520
We've gained a whole slew of soldiers to add to our side.

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:10.010
That's awesome!

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:15.520
I'll be on my way. There's still plenty of areas that have yet to ally with us.

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:17.890
All right. Good luck!

00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:23.230
If your negotiations with Delzaine fail, call for us right away.

00:13:23.230 --> 00:13:24.870
We'll come immediately.

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:28.470
Thanks, but hopefully it will never come to that.

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:30.410
Well then, goodbye.

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:36.310
It's sure going to get busy around here.

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:38.540
Lords and the Zoozians...

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:42.080
Now that we have this much power...

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:45.490
Emilio...

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:04.040
I don't have a choice.

00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:07.910
This is the only way I know how to live...

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:09.340
Louise?

00:14:14.420 --> 00:14:16.420
What's with the scary face?

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:18.580
Nothing. It doesn't matter.

00:14:23.060 --> 00:14:26.230
If there's a problem, you should let it be heard.

00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:29.930
I was just thinking about Eljuia's omen.

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:32.700
True, it's on my mind, too.

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:36.400
By the way, we just got word from the other crew.

00:14:36.400 --> 00:14:40.400
They're gathering loads of support from the lords all over.

00:14:41.410 --> 00:14:42.810
I'm sorry...

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:47.550
Emilio! Shun!

00:14:47.550 --> 00:14:48.650
Hey. Good morning.

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:49.550
What is it?

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:51.090
Have you heard?!

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:55.460
The Ignauts went all around and rallied up a bunch of new allies to join us!

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:57.290
Yeah, I heard already.

00:14:58.290 --> 00:14:59.460
Aww...

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:02.730
Actually, I was the first one to hear the news.

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:06.600
When the report came in, everyone else was sound asleep.

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:12.440
So were you, by the way. Until you came stumbling out like a sleepwalking dimwit.

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:14.240
Wh-Who are you calling a dimwit?!

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:16.680
You had a stream of drool hanging off your face.

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:17.480
You're kidding?!

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:19.250
I am.

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:20.580
You little...

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:25.320
You two never change.
I can never tell if you get along or not.

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:28.620
Who cares how stupid you look when waking up?

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:34.500
I care! Take it back!
I'm handsome all around the clock!

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:37.700
With the lords and the Zoozians...

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:40.100
...we've accumulated a sizable force.

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:45.510
Even if we can't face Delzaine head on, if everything goes right...

00:15:45.510 --> 00:15:46.370
Emilio...

00:15:46.370 --> 00:15:50.540
You... still intend to kill Delzaine?

00:15:52.310 --> 00:15:55.680
Of course. I will avenge my father.

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:59.050
That's the one reason I've held onto my hatred for all these years.

00:15:59.050 --> 00:16:00.060
But--

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:05.290
Someone has to! Someone has to cleanse the regret of my father...

00:16:05.290 --> 00:16:09.060
That's why I went so far as to give up my place as the prince!

00:16:09.060 --> 00:16:11.700
You... You think you know everything!

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:14.200
Shut up! I--

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.170
This has nothing to do with you.

00:16:16.170 --> 00:16:17.210
Huh?

00:16:17.210 --> 00:16:19.310
It doesn't? Since when?

00:16:19.310 --> 00:16:23.710
When you return to the surface, you're gone for good. You're just an outsider!

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:27.820
Endora's... our problems don't even matter to you!

00:16:27.820 --> 00:16:29.340
You piece of--!

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:33.490
Stop it!

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:36.390
Did you ever think people might worry about you?!

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:42.330
Remember Falarion? Are you forgetting everything Alicia's father said?!

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:48.740
If you're that consumed by hatred, you'll get yourself trapped in a Warp Relic!

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:51.740
Are you fine with that? Losing yourself?

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:54.680
I... won't let that happen.

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:57.350
How can you be so sure?

00:16:57.350 --> 00:16:59.580
Enough! Let go!

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:01.020
You little--!

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:04.920
Quit it!

00:17:17.270 --> 00:17:19.430
You think your problems aren't my concern?

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:20.870
I...

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:26.140
Not once have I thought that to myself.

00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:29.580
Shun!

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:36.880
I can't... I can't give up anymore.

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:39.790
Emilio...

00:17:44.260 --> 00:17:48.500
I knew it... This data makes it clear as day.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:52.800
Warp Particles are decreasing all throughout Endora.

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:57.470
The situation is worse than
I imagined. But how can this be?

00:17:57.470 --> 00:18:03.970
If the Warp Particles keep diminishing at this rate, Endora itself will come crashing down...

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:12.790
Aren't those the Warp Particle measurements taken in the past?

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:14.320
Have you noticed something?

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:17.360
Well, the decrease in Warp Particles seems to begin around

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:21.160
the same time as
King Delzaine took the throne.

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:22.260
You're right!

00:18:22.260 --> 00:18:27.340
Are the dwindling Warp Particles and the King's induction somehow related or a mere coincidence?

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:31.670
No, everything happens for a reason.
If we can only discover the correlation...

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:36.340
Like the motion of a swimming fish, its vibrations reach out and...

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:40.620
The only one who knows what happened when the King took the throne...

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:42.350
...is the King himself.

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:47.290
It seems like I'll have to venture to Babylon myself.

00:18:47.290 --> 00:18:49.280
But can I make it in time?

00:18:58.970 --> 00:19:00.640
Oh?

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:04.310
Quite impressive! This is a nice little lab you've got here...

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:08.680
Right? It wasn't easy getting all this equipment here.

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:15.220
I had a hunch that the chief and King Delzaine were delving into shady practices.

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:20.350
Ever since then, I've done all my personal research secretly in here.

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:23.660
We scientists must distance ourselves from authority

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:30.730
to pursue the pure and authentic truth, just like you have, Pascal.

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:34.600
You won't be able to reach Babylon any faster than using this.

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:36.040
Oh?

00:19:37.840 --> 00:19:40.440
The chief doesn't even know I've made this.

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:43.240
Sometimes we scientists have to be sneaky.

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:48.010
Let's hurry. The King may be entering Babylon as we speak...

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:04.270
The time has come.

00:20:04.270 --> 00:20:06.460
Open the door to the surface!

00:20:20.620 --> 00:20:21.380
Shun.

00:20:21.380 --> 00:20:23.620
What do you want?

00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:25.450
I may have said too much.

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:30.290
Huh? Um... Sorry for hitting you, too.

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:32.760
But I still haven't changed my mind.

00:20:32.760 --> 00:20:35.330
I will avenge him.

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:36.630
You're still on about that?

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:38.100
It's in view now!

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:41.940
It's Babylon.

00:20:46.810 --> 00:20:49.980
So this... is Babylon?

00:20:49.980 --> 00:20:51.910
We're finally here.

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:04.930
"To be continued..."

00:21:05.590 --> 00:21:09.630
<i>Took a long way to get here</i>

00:21:09.630 --> 00:21:13.600
<i>Had to go around and around</i>

00:21:13.600 --> 00:21:17.710
<i>But every single road I've taken</i>

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:21.610
<i>Made me who I am today</i>

00:21:21.610 --> 00:21:28.540
<i>go my way go my way</i>

00:21:30.820 --> 00:21:40.030
<i>The world will show you there's tomorrow</i>

00:21:40.030 --> 00:21:48.560
<i>Look up to the blue sky and you will see</i>

00:21:49.400 --> 00:21:57.480
<i>I try to be better than who I was yesterday</i>

00:21:57.480 --> 00:22:04.650
<i>So I can see you with a smile on my face today</i>

00:22:04.650 --> 00:22:09.890
<i>Now what should we get into today?</i>

00:22:09.890 --> 00:22:18.530
<i>The scent of summer arouses my heart</i>

00:22:18.530 --> 00:22:23.670
<i>And I can't seem to find the right words to tell you</i>

00:22:23.670 --> 00:22:28.110
<i>That I love you just the way you are</i>

00:22:35.180 --> 00:22:39.940
"Episode 11: Depths"

00:22:37.590 --> 00:22:39.920
Next episode, "Depths."
